From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ROCKNIX <info@rocknix.org>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] target: add ROCKNIX target specifications for aarch64, arm,
 and x86_64

Add three new Rust target specifications for ROCKNIX. These targets
replace the previous JSON-based custom target definitions (targets/*.json
+ RUST_TARGET_PATH), which rustc >= 1.95 rejects on the stable channel
("custom targets are unstable and require -Zunstable-options").

Targets added:
  - aarch64-rocknix-linux-gnu
  - arm-rocknix-linux-gnueabihf
  - x86_64-rocknix-linux-gnu

Each target is based on its corresponding upstream Linux GNU target and
inherits all defaults from base::linux_gnu::opts(), with the overrides
from the previous ROCKNIX JSON specs applied:

aarch64-rocknix-linux-gnu:
  - supported_sanitizers: ADDRESS | CFI | LEAK | MEMORY | MEMTAG | THREAD | HWADDRESS
    (drops KCFI and REALTIME, as in the JSON spec)
  - supports_xray: false

arm-rocknix-linux-gnueabihf:
  - features: +strict-align,+v6,+vfp2,-d32
    (-d32 keeps only 16 double-precision VFP registers, as in the JSON spec)

x86_64-rocknix-linux-gnu:
  - stack_probes: Call (upstream: Inline, as in the JSON spec)
  - supported_sanitizers: ADDRESS | CFI | LEAK | MEMORY | THREAD
    (drops KCFI, DATAFLOW, SAFESTACK, REALTIME, as in the JSON spec)
  - supports_xray: false

All three targets are registered in supported_targets! in
compiler/rustc_target/src/spec/mod.rs.

Ported from the LibreELEC equivalent
(packages/rust/rust/patches/9999-target-add-LibreELEC-target-specifications-for-aarch.patch),
which was introduced for the same rust >= 1.95 restriction.

Metadata:
  - tier: 3 (community-maintained, not part of official Rust CI)
  - host_tools: false
  - std: true
---
